('battle-bomb-42', 'bomb', 'battle', 'Defuse Duel', 'game', 1, array['duel_pistol','duel_smg']::text[], 'A device is ticking. Scout can see it, Decoder holds the bomb manual, Intel has a special order from HQ. Agree on ONE wire and cut it.', '{"scout":{"title":"The device","body":"Wires from the TOP: White, Black, Black, Red, Yellow.\nSerial number: TN51Q9.  LED: RED.","game":{"type":"bomb","wires":["white","black","black","red","yellow"],"serial":"TN51Q9","led":"red"}},"decoder":{"title":"Bomb manual","body":"1. More than one RED wire → cut the LAST red wire.\n2. Otherwise, if the serial number ends in an ODD digit and there is a BLUE wire → cut the FIRST blue wire.\n3. Otherwise, if the LED is GREEN → cut the LAST wire.\n4. Otherwise, if there is no YELLOW wire → cut the SECOND wire.\n5. Otherwise → cut the FIRST wire."},"intel":{"title":"Order from HQ (check first!)","body":"If there are exactly two BLACK wires, cut the FIRST black wire — ignore the manual."}}'::jsonb, '[{"label":"Wire to cut (number from the top)","accept":["2"]}]'::jsonb, false, 3, 80, 'Intel first: does HQ''s order apply? If not, Decoder walks down the manual from rule 1. Scout describes every wire top to bottom.', 'white,black,black,red,yellow · TN51Q9 · red → override: If there are exactly two BLACK wires, cut the FIRST black wire — ignore the manual. → wire 2', null, 25, 'published'),
